# os-release - SYSKRNL distro metadata (rd vms-700/vms-296/vms-3de)
#
# GNU/Linux-style dual identity: this file describes the SYSKRNL layer (the
# Linux kernel underneath OVMX's product runs on), never the product itself.
# It follows the freedesktop.org os-release(5) convention every Linux
# distribution ships at /etc/os-release, so standard Linux tooling
# (systemd, package managers, `uname`-adjacent scripts) that inspects this
# file sees an honest answer about the SYSKRNL layer (the Linux kernel).
#
# The VMS-compatible PRODUCT identity ("OpenVMX V0.3 - OpenVMS-compatible")
# is a SEPARATE, VMS-facing surface -- SHOW SYSTEM, MONITOR, the DCL login
# banner, sourced from src/libvms/include/ovmx_identity.h
# (OVMX_PRODUCT_BANNER). It is deliberately NOT duplicated here: a VMS
# session never reads this file (INV-4 -- no Linux leak on a VMS-facing
# surface), and this file never claims to be the VMS-compatible product.
#
# NAME/VERSION_ID here are hand-maintained text, not generated from the
# identity SSOT (this file predates any process boots enough Linux to run
# a generator) -- keep VERSION_ID in step with OVMX_PRODUCT_VERSION in
# ovmx_identity.h by hand when that changes.
NAME="OVMX/Linux"
ID=ovmx
PRETTY_NAME="OVMX/Linux"
VERSION="0.3 (SYSKRNL)"
VERSION_ID="0.3"
HOME_URL="https://openvmx.3dl.dev"
